    {"path": "tools/campaign.py", "role": "campaign driver: freezes the kernel choice, then measures it, and records the machine both ran on", "classification": "source", "reproduction_command": "make x86-tune && make x86-measure X86_FLAGS=--campaign", "required": true},
    {"path": "results/v2/x86", "role": "x86 complete-CTR measurement campaign (env.json, kat.json, tuning.json, runs.csv, summary.csv). PENDING: deferred until a quiet machine and not yet produced; this host is bimodal. Until it lands, results/speed.csv (and results/wide-speed-r4.csv, results/wide-speed-r5.csv) remain the current x86 figures, measuring the round function rather than complete CTR.", "classification": "measured", "reproduction_command": "make x86-tune && git commit results/v2/x86/tuning.json && make x86-measure X86_FLAGS=--campaign", "required": false},
    {"path": "results/v2/a7", "role": "CURRENT A7 result: Cortex-A7 (ARMv7-A, 32-bit) complete counter-mode campaign over SSH (env.json, kat.json, tuning.json, runs.csv, summary.csv); measured with a governor/clock gate and a thermal guard, paired within-run ratios against present-80-r16. Supersedes results/speed-arm.csv and results/wide-speed-arm.csv for achievable throughput.", "classification": "measured", "reproduction_command": "python3 tools/campaign.py a7 --host a7 --tune && git commit results/v2/a7/tuning.json && python3 tools/campaign.py a7 --host a7 --measure --campaign", "required": true},
    {"path": "results/v2/m4", "role": "CURRENT M4 result: Cortex-M4 (STM32F407) complete counter-mode campaign (env.json, kat.json, tuning.json, runs.csv, summary.csv); deterministic DWT cycle counts across memory configurations, the source of the complete-CTR 12 Mbit/s verdict. Supersedes results/m4-speed.csv for achievable throughput.", "classification": "measured", "reproduction_command": "python3 tools/campaign.py m4 --tune && git commit results/v2/m4/tuning.json fw/m4/ctr_winners.mk && python3 tools/campaign.py m4 --measure", "required": true},
    {"path": "results/v2/cuda", "role": "CURRENT CUDA result set: GPU block-evaluation (block-eval.csv) and master-key search (master-key-search.csv), all seven constructions, on an RTX 5070 Laptop. Supersedes results/gpu-speed*.csv, renaming the block-evaluation metric from tests/s. PENDING a quiet-machine campaign: both files currently carry `# provenance: SMOKE-RUN` and must not be quoted until re-run overwrites the marker with CAMPAIGN.", "classification": "measured", "reproduction_command": "make gpu-bench-v2 GPU_V2_FLAGS=--campaign", "required": false},
    {"path": "results/speed.csv", "role": "64-bit speed measurements", "classification": "measured", "reproduction_command": "taskset -c 2 ./build/bench --csv results/speed.csv", "required": true},
